s based in Morton Grove, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Julie  Smolyansky | Chairperson of the Board, CEO, President & Secretary | Age 50 | Compensation: $2.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 293 people. Revenue per employee of $725K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Defensive peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $7K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Lifeway Foods, Inc. is a small-cap consumer defensive business with a $327M market cap on $212M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 17% against a 9% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, with gross margins sitting at 26%.","The company is burning through $16M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 39% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 131% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3145573957596564},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (11.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $3.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-3372291.81},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Consumer Defensive peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Slow-motion taste and channel shifts \u2014 private label, Gen-Z health preferences, or a DTC disruption can erode decade-old brand moats without a single dramatic quarter.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 and health-trend demand destruction \u2014 weight-loss drugs and wellness shifts are structurally reducing consumption in snack, beverage, and packaged food categories.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 17% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Growing faster than most Consumer Defensive peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Consumer Defensive sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 11% over 3 months","Consumer Defensive ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Consumer Defensive tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Lifeway Foods (NASDAQ:LWAY) Major Shareholder Edward Smolyansky Sells 70,000 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/lifeway-foods-nasdaqlway-major-shareholder-edward-smolyansky-sells-70000-shares-of-stock.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793965136.0,"origin":"tiingo","sent