imate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Consumer Defensive peers: P/E 31.4 vs 18.5 and EV/EBITDA 17.5 vs 10.3 (sector median).","The EBIT multiple is close to its own 10-year median (-8%).","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of -5.0% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.6% (vs the 8% bar).","The 3 covering analysts target $33.00 on average, 52% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 17% clears the cost of capital of 9.2% by 8pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.01).","It runs a 26% gross margin and burns cash (FCF margin -8%).","Earnings quality is a concern: cash conversion of only 0.79x.","ROE of 16% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.2x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 13.8, in the safe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.23).","The Beneish M-score (-2.13) sits just under the manipulation line, so earnings quality bears watching."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 14.5% over 3 years, 15.8% over 5 years and 4.5% over 10 years, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 13%).","At current returns, reinvesting 100% of profits supports about 16.8% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Capex runs 6.9x depreciation (12.9% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth.","Its Rule of 40 score is 7, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 39.2%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 57%.","Insider trading is two-way: 7 purchases and 13 sales over the past year, net $3.4M sold.","Short interest is elevated at 11.0% of the float, 4.2 days to cover."],"people":["With about 293 employees, each generates about $725K of revenue, 1.4x the Consumer Defensive median, and productivity has risen 8.3% a year.","Free cash flow is negative, at -$56K per employee.","CEO pay is $2.6M (4x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $7K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":59,"head":"Avoid: priced 131% above its fair value of $9.35.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 48, gates 13/26)","ROIC 16.8% vs WACC 9.2%","Revenue grew 15.8%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA -0.3x","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["Trades 131% above fair value of $9.35","FCF margin 7.7% (burns cash)","P/E 31.4x vs sector 18.5x","EV/EBITDA 17.5x vs sector 10.3x","Heavy insider selling ($3.4M net over 12 months)"],"flags":["Priced 131% above its fair value of $9.35"],"need":[],"buy_below":7.95,"vc":{"base":9.35,"base_src":"blend","bear":null,"bull":null,"alt_median":9.35,"n_alt":2,"gap":null,"dispersion":0.4681,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (47% dispersion)"]},"med":{"pe":18.5188,"ev_ebitda":10.2635,"pfcf":15.9681,"pb":2.0792,"roic":0.1185,"gross_margin":0.3401,"fcf_margin":0.0601,"div_yield":0.0296}},"ticker":"LWAY","date":"2026-11-06"}